      "mergeID": "5d43f6ebc42a66254928dbdf",
      "mergedPostDetails": "On Oculus, when you slowly close your hands you can now only close them a little bit until they snap shut in to a fist. Instead of being able to smoothly close them all the way. Very important to me and in terms of body language/immersion.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Oculus Rift hand issue",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5d24813a36ba4f2b571ec9e1",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I think that's a SteamVR issue. Yesterday with the newest VRChat update (Build 825) I didn't have any issues. Today after SteamVR update 1.6.10 I have the exact same issue you are reporting.\n\nThis only happens if you are playing through SteamVR, I had a friend try to replicate it on the Oculus Store client and he didn't have that issue.\n\nStrangely enough the SteamVR dashboard correctly displays the grip button being pressed. The effect is only noticeable in-game.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
